{"nodeSize":{"w":190,"h":58},"bounds":{"x":-90,"y":-90,"w":3134,"h":1234},"areas":[{"n":1,"title":"The corpus arrives","body":"Two folders, two sensitivity labels. **The folder a PDF sits in decides whether it is PUBLIC literature or an INTERNAL lab notebook** \u2014 the label is structural, not a field somebody has to remember to fill in. That single decision is what later lets the agent answer from the literature in public while keeping the notebooks behind the identity check.","x":368,"y":0,"w":830,"h":230},{"n":2,"title":"Nothing is indexed twice","body":"The MD5 of each file is compared against the hashes already registered, and a Merge in *keep non-matches* mode drops whatever is already in. So **re-running the ingestion over the whole folder is safe and nearly free**: only genuinely new files reach the embedder. Without this, every re-run would duplicate 87,765 chunks and quietly poison retrieval with near-identical neighbours.","x":1348,"y":0,"w":544,"h":230},{"n":3,"title":"Split, embed, store","body":"Recursive splitter at **1,200 characters with 250 of overlap**, then a single embeddings node: `bge-m3` running locally in Ollama, 1,024 dimensions. One node and not two, deliberately \u2014 if the indexing side and the query side ever embedded with different models, the vector store would return nonsense **without raising a single error**. Sharing the node makes that failure impossible rather than unlikely.","x":2042,"y":0,"w":544,"h":334},{"n":4,"title":"Who is asking","body":"Before a single token reaches a model: identify the caller, check them against the researcher whitelist, and branch. **A denied request is logged and answered** \u2014 it does not fail silently. This is the same gate the ingestion workflow uses, and it is the reason the agent can be exposed to anyone at all.","x":0,"y":464,"w":1402,"h":230},{"n":5,"title":"The agent, and its understudy","body":"Gemini answers. If it fails \u2014 quota, outage, anything \u2014 the error output routes to a **second, complete Agent node** wired to Qwen3 14B running locally. n8n's Agent node refuses two language models on one node, so the fallback had to be built at workflow level instead of inside it; that was found by trying twice and reading the error. Every exchange is logged before the reply goes back.","x":1552,"y":464,"w":1402,"h":230},{"n":6,"title":"Nine tools, and one switched off","body":"**The agent never writes SQL.** Every tool is a call to a stored function with typed parameters, so what it can ask is bounded by the database rather than by the prompt. Six read the laboratory, one reads the schema dictionary, one searches the literature semantically, two walk the knowledge graph. The Cohere reranker sits wired but **disabled on purpose**: it is the one component that would send chunk text to a third party.","x":776,"y":824,"w":1402,"h":230}],"nodes":[{"id":"\u25b6 Run Ingestion","name":"\u25b6 Run Ingestion","kind":"trigger","disabled":false,"area":1,"x":402,"y":86},{"id":"Read PUBLIC Corpus","name":"Read PUBLIC Corpus","kind":"file","disabled":false,"area":1,"x":688,"y":34},{"id":"Read INTERNAL Corpus","name":"Read INTERNAL Corpus","kind":"file","disabled":false,"area":1,"x":688,"y":138},{"id":"Label PUBLIC","name":"Label PUBLIC","kind":"transform","disabled":false,"area":1,"x":974,"y":34},{"id":"Label INTERNAL","name":"Label INTERNAL","kind":"transform","disabled":false,"area":1,"x":974,"y":138},{"id":"Compute File MD5","name":"Compute File MD5","kind":"code","disabled":false,"area":2,"x":1382,"y":34},{"id":"Already Indexed Hashes","name":"Already Indexed Hashes","kind":"db","disabled":false,"area":2,"x":1382,"y":138},{"id":"Discard Already Indexed","name":"Discard Already Indexed","kind":"merge","disabled":false,"area":2,"x":1668,"y":86},{"id":"Insert into pgvector","name":"Insert into pgvector","kind":"vector","disabled":false,"area":3,"x":2362,"y":86},{"id":"Register in rag_documents","name":"Register in rag_documents","kind":"db","disabled":false,"area":3,"x":2362,"y":190},{"id":"Document Loader","name":"Document Loader","kind":"file","disabled":false,"area":3,"x":2076,"y":138},{"id":"Split Text (Chunking)","name":"Split Text (Chunking)","kind":"transform","disabled":false,"area":3,"x":2076,"y":34},{"id":"Embeddings bge-m3 (Local Ollama)","name":"Embeddings bge-m3 (Local Ollama)","kind":"embed","disabled":false,"area":3,"x":2076,"y":242},{"id":"Chat: Ask the Lab","name":"Chat: Ask the Lab","kind":"trigger","disabled":false,"area":4,"x":34,"y":550},{"id":"Agent - ALCheMy Lab Assistant","name":"Agent - ALCheMy Lab Assistant","kind":"ai","disabled":false,"area":5,"x":1872,"y":550},{"id":"Chat Model","name":"Chat Model","kind":"model","disabled":false,"area":5,"x":1586,"y":498},{"id":"Conversation Memory","name":"Conversation Memory","kind":"memory","disabled":false,"area":5,"x":1586,"y":602},{"id":"search_documentation","name":"search_documentation","kind":"vector","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":1096,"y":962},{"id":"Reranker (Cohere) - DISABLED","name":"Reranker (Cohere) - DISABLED","kind":"rerank","disabled":true,"area":6,"x":1954,"y":962},{"id":"read_data_dictionary","name":"read_data_dictionary","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":810,"y":962},{"id":"search_synthesis","name":"search_synthesis","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":810,"y":858},{"id":"get_characterisation","name":"get_characterisation","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":1096,"y":858},{"id":"sample_summary","name":"sample_summary","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":1382,"y":858},{"id":"statistics","name":"statistics","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":1668,"y":858},{"id":"search_library","name":"search_library","kind":"tool","disabled":false,"area":6,"x":1954,"y":858},{"id":"Identify Caller","name":"Identify Caller","kind":"transform","disabled":false,"area":4,"x":320,"y":550},{"id":"Authorise Caller","name":"Authorise Caller","kind":"db","disabled":false,"area":4,"x":606,"y":550},{"id":"Is Caller Allow